## Intent

Make /calm a persistent, compact live presentation mode in the Firstmate Pi extension while preserving all underlying operational behavior. The selected Calm state must persist per Firstmate home across process restarts and resumed sessions; Pi's native Working... indicator must remain visible; Calm must not add any persistent transcript or footer status; and hidden operational rows must consume zero vertical space without blank gaps. Preserve model context, watcher behavior, Ahoy, expansion state, and complete export/share session artifacts, including full hidden operational text in serialized session data and Pi's sidebar tree, while the main exported message transcript may omit hidden operational custom messages. Treat the current static exact operational envelopes as sufficient provenance, accepting copy-paste risk and adding no nonce, source-authentication, replay prevention, secondary token, blocking, redaction, or private retrieval machinery. Keep non-Pi harness behavior unchanged, document the home-local config/calm contract and export semantics accurately, and cover the four fixed UI outcomes with deterministic and real Pi regressions.

