## Intent

Collapse firstmate's separate 'decisions' concept into the one primitive the captain cares about: a decision is simply a task waiting on the captain - an ordinary backlog task held for the captain (tasks-axi hold --kind captain), identified by its task id. Captain-approved simplification grounded in two investigation reports (data/decisions-concept-ripout-investigation-s1, data/fm-decision-hold-noise-investigation-s1) which found the old decision type (the <origin>-decision-<key> derived identity, the kind==captain projection filter, and the ~900-line bin/fm-decision-hold.sh) recorded which script created a row rather than what the captain has to do, and misclassified live data in both directions - surfacing noise AND hiding real captain-blocked work. All in ONE PR, per the captain's direction.

Requirements in their accepted form:
1. The distinct decision type/identity goes away. bin/fm-captain-hold.sh replaces bin/fm-decision-hold.sh as the single owner of the surviving mechanics: guarded hold creation (create-or-hold, idempotent, --until deferral dates), the recorded-answer close (answer, with --release to free a captain-gated WORK item instead of completing it), the one channel-agnostic keyed-answer intake (answers + bind/unbind/binding; keys are task ids; optional 4th tab column carries a card-declared close mode done|release), and the investigation completion gate (complete/verify).
2. Exactly two safety behaviors survive, attached to the plain captain-held task: (a) an investigation or visual review may NOT be torn down while the captain's open questions live only in its report - the complete/verify gate wired into scout teardown; (b) nothing the captain owns may be closed without recording what he actually said - the resolution record with digest idempotency, drift refusal, and retroactive recording for out-of-band closes (old repair semantics folded into answer).
3. The fleet snapshot and bearings respect deferral: parse tasks-axi hold-until (previously ignored entirely); captain_actionable = queued + hold-kind captain + unblocked + due, INDEPENDENT of row kind; date-deferred holds render as Charted Next gates with an 'until <date>:' reason and resurface on their date; prose-deferred rows (the pre-existing SUPERSEDED/NOT REQUIRED/DEFERRED marker set, extended from body-only to hold reason, computed once in the canonical snapshot as deferred_marker) leave the default decisions and gates views with an omitted[] disclosure, revealed by --all-decisions/--all-queued, except that a dated future hold always renders as a dated gate; Recently Landed excludes rows that closed while still captain-held (surviving hold-kind annotations on Done rows) instead of excluding kind==captain, so a work item released before completion lands normally.
4. Migration is first-class; existing installs keep working on day one with nothing lost to the captain: legacy <origin>-decision-<key> rows are already plain task ids and work unchanged through every surface; pre-collapse decision_keys= metadata short keys resolve through the legacy composed identity; a concrete-origin binding composes legacy channel keys; old resolution records are recognized wherever a record is read; bin/fm-decision-hold.sh remains for ONE release as a thin compat shim mapping every retired subcommand (id/hold/complete/verify/resolve/answer/decline/repair/answers/bind/unbind/binding) onto fm-captain-hold.sh so in-flight pre-collapse briefs keep working; the PR body must note that running homes pick up the instruction surface via the normal update path.
5. Every consumer is preserved through the collapse: bin/fm-teardown.sh's scout verify gate; bin/fm-send.sh --resolve-key (status-ledger close unchanged; the hold fallback now resolves the key as a task id first, then the legacy composed identity, and feeds resolved ids to the intake); bin/fm-procevent.sh's binding/answers feed seam (CLI shape deliberately unchanged); bin/fm-procevent-lavish.sh answers (now relays the card-declared close mode, only from rows tagged choice); bin/fm-bearings-board.sh (binds the collapsed intake; the fm-bearings-board.v1 payload gains an optional per-card close: 'done'|'release' field, validated fail-closed, and the template forwards it in the answer context); the status-ledger needs-decision:/blocked:/resolved:/captain-held keyed flow in fm-classify-lib.sh is deliberately untouched.
6. Policy surface trimmed to match: new .agents/skills/captain-hold-lifecycle (short collapsed policy: prefer holding the work item the question gates, one held task per genuine gate rather than a row per question, 'later' is recorded as an --until date, never close without the captain's words); the old decision-hold-lifecycle skill becomes a pointer stub kept one release for in-flight briefs; AGENTS.md sections 2/7/10/13 updated to the one-primitive statement; the bearings skill updated (card key = the captain-held task id, card typing is composer judgment since no backlog field types cards, gate-shaped cards declare close: release); docs/decision-hold-lifecycle.md replaced by docs/captain-hold-lifecycle.md; docs/scripts.md, docs/configuration.md, docs/verification/process-event-sources.md updated; fm-brief.sh scaffolds point at the new skill.
