Deliberate decisions a diff-only reviewer would otherwise flag: the metadata attestation keeps the historical decisions_reviewed=1 / decision_keys= key names for compatibility with existing on-disk task metadata and the backend test fixtures that write them (entries are now task ids; legacy short entries resolve via origin composition, exact-task-id match wins). complete no longer enforces a per-status-key inventory mapping: with a non-empty verified inventory it transfers EVERY still-open keyed status decision to that inventory (the old per-key forcing produced the 28-holds-from-one-review pathology the reports document), while --none is still refused whenever lifecycle-open status decisions exist. answer closes a task even when work is routed behind it, because a Done blocker reads as resolved everywhere; the old routed 'resolve' path is retired and the shim maps it to answer plus recording the routed ids in the decision text and clearing the edges. The resolution block is written at the TOP of the body via --body-file with tasks-axi --archive-body, preserving the previous body below it so a released work item keeps its plan. A re-held task accepts a NEW answer as a new record on top; an interrupted-close retry has its recorded close mode checked so a retry cannot silently flip a release into a completion. The intake refuses to retro-record on already-closed items (reported skipped) except for an idempotent replay of the identical answer. hold no longer sets a kind on created tasks - kind is deliberately meaningless to captain surfaces now. Adding hold-until to the title metadata-stripping pattern also fixes a pre-existing bug where a dated row leaked '(hold-until: ...)' into its parsed title.

