## Intent

https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/6357 Needs to be rebased and have its conflicts resolved. It also needs to somehow trigger a re-review from kunchenguid's firstmate.

Context: PR 6357 ("fix(bearings): stop truncating Charted Next titles and reasons on the lavish board") is open from the fork branch jesstelford/firstmate `fm/fm-board-charted-no-truncate` (head 02a2bedb) and GitHub reports it CONFLICTING with kunchenguid/firstmate main. kunchenguid's firstmate triages PRs by comment ("Speaking as Kun's firstmate") and left it `waiting-author` because the head had no no-mistakes pipeline attestation (its "Require no-mistakes" check failed); its note says to re-raise via no-mistakes. Greptile also reviewed it.

Rebase onto latest `main` and fix the CI failure. (Referring to https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/6357, whose "Full suite" CI check failed on head 14d53b31.)

## What Changed

- `fm-bearings-snapshot.sh` adds a `--fields gate-text` option. It adds `title_full` and `reason_full` to every gate row, including the return-catchup and main-inventory rows. Their text is untruncated, with only whitespace collapsed. The bounded `title` and `reason` still feed the chat digest. Without the option, `title_full` and `reason_full` are removed and the hidden-surfaces list points to `--fields gate-text`.
- `fm-fleet-snapshot.sh` no longer cuts secondmate queued `title`, `blocked_reason` and `hold_reason` to 120/160 characters in the home summary. It only collapses whitespace, so the full text reaches the board. The summary's byte cap still limits these fields.
- The board template gives Charted Next rows a new `bb-row--full` style. Titles and reasons wrap in full instead of being cut off with an ellipsis, and the picker and badge line up with the first title line. The bearings skill and the `fm-bearings-board.sh` payload contract now say to fill row `title`/`reason` from the full-text fields. New tests in `tests/fm-bearings-snapshot.test.sh` and `tests/fm-bearings-board-render.test.sh` check this.

