Both bearings test suites pass. They cover the board renderer, including a real-Chrome layout check at phone and desktop widths, and the snapshot's `--fields gate-text` and untruncated secondmate summary. I also built a real board with long Charted Next rows and screenshotted it at 500px and 1280px: full titles and reasons wrap with nothing clipped, and the badges and checkboxes line up with the first line. The PR's 'Full suite' CI failure turned out to be the maintainer-only `full-ci` label gate, not a code problem.

